# - {lle_present: false}
# - {lat_present: false}
# - {lat_note: 'HAS_LAT=False in grb_sample.ecsv; GCN 12801 quotes a LAT boresight angle of 84 deg and poshist gives theta_LATz = 87.2-87.9
#     deg across the source window - the burst was outside the LAT FoV, so the absence of LLE/LAT data is expected, not a gap'}
# - {d1_theta_check: 'APPLIED. All four responses are single-matrix, so per D1 the interval test is not decisive and the off-axis-angle
#     test governs. Per-detector angles recomputed from the poshist quaternions using the pipeline own primitive scripts/00_prototype_one_burst.py::get_detector_angle
#     at the source-window start, middle and end.'}
# - {d1_result: 'max |delta theta| over the stamped source window = 0.64 deg (n3); n4 0.18, n5 -0.28, b0 -0.29. Far inside the D1 tolerance
#     (<=4 deg fine; >=15 deg invalid). Angles at T0 reproduce the stamped DET_ANGLE values to 0.01 deg.'}
# - {d1_validity_horizon: 'the same single-matrix DRMs drift past 4 deg (n3) only near t ~ +95 s: +90 s gives 3.83 deg, +120 s gives 5.10
#     deg. Any future refit of THIS burst with a window extending beyond ~+90 s must regenerate the responses.'}
# - {rsp_interval_note: 'the .rsp headers advertise TSTART/TSTOP = trigtime -136.19 / +478.22 s, which brackets the source window, so
#     the naive interval test also passes - but that is not what earns the PASS (D1): the spacecraft rocks through ~26 deg of n3 angle
#     inside that advertised span.'}
# - {d4_note: 'PRE-TRIGGER EMISSION EXISTS. GBM catalog T90_START = -11.520 s; Golkhou+2015 T_start,100 = -25.674 s; GCN 12799 (BAT) reports
#     a weak peak from BAT T0 to T+20 s = GBM -28.2 to -8.2 s, plus a possible 3-4 sigma precursor near GBM -98 s. The trigger time is
#     NOT the burst start: GBM triggered 28.24 s after Swift-BAT, on the MAIN pulse.'}
# - {qc_flag_new: "BKG_NEG [-30, -8] s OVERLAPS the BAT-detected weak first peak (GBM clock -28.2 to -8.2 s). bn120102095 is NOT in results/human_review_qc_flags.txt,\
#     \ so this is a NEW observation, not an accepted decision. For comparison the GBM catalog own pre-burst background is [-32.0, -28.5]\
#     \ s, i.e. it stops short of that region; Burgess 2019 \xA72 records modifying catalog backgrounds generically for on-source contamination.\
#     \ RAISED FOR VIKAS - not acted on: Stage-1 flags are decisions and this selection is human-approved."}
# - {verdict: 'PASS (responses) + FLAG (background window). All 4 approved detectors resolve to a real response file under the correct
#     naming, and every response is valid over the stamped source window by the off-axis-angle test (max delta theta 0.64 deg). Separately
#     flagged: possible source contamination of the negative background interval - a selection question, not a response problem.'}
